<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Honorius III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1150–<a href="/years/1227">1227</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Cencio Savelli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honorius">Honorius</a> III reigned from 1216 to 1227. He confirmed the Dominican order in 1216 and the Franciscan rule in 1223, and promoted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifth-crusade">Fifth Crusade</a>. In 1217 he sent a royal crown to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-the-first-crowned">Stefan Nemanjić</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, who became known as Stefan the First-Crowned, marking the start of the medieval Serbian kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-honorius-iii.jpg" alt="Pope Honorius III" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hegesandros · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pope_Honorious_III_kneeling_at_feet_of_Christ.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>With the bull Religiosam vitam, <b>Pope Honorius III</b> gave universal recognition to the Order of Preachers founded by the Castilian priest Dominic de Guzmán.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-22">22 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In the bull Vineae Domini custodes, <b>Pope Honorius III</b> approved a mission to Morocco, then part of the Almohad empire, asked for by the friars Dominic of Segovia and Martin.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-10">10 June in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Following the death of <b>Pope Honorius III</b>, Ugolino di Conti was elected pope and took the name Gregory IX.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-19">19 March in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Pope Honorius III</b> crowned Frederick II emperor in St Peter's.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-22">22 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Nemanja abdicated in 1196 in favour of his son Stefan, who received a royal crown from <b>Pope Honorius III</b> in 1217.</blockquote><a href="/state/grand-principality-of-serbia">Grand Principality of Serbia</a></li><li><blockquote>Stefan, son of Stefan Nemanja and ruler of the Grand Principality of Serbia, was crowned king in 1217 with a crown sent by <b>Pope Honorius III</b>, earning the name Stefan the First-Crowned.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-serbia-medieval">Kingdom of Serbia (medieval)</a></li></ul></section>
